# Line endings are part of the contract here, not a preference.
#
# Found by the first Windows CI run (2026-08-18). There was no .gitattributes,
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, so a fresh checkout on the
# windows-latest runner rewrote every file to CRLF. The self verification corpus
# searches for multi line code fragments written with \n, so every one of them
# matched nothing:
#
#   E_SELFVERIFY_FIXTURE_DIRTY  { mutantId: 'delete_orphan_child_rows',
#                                 findCount: 0, replacementCount: 0 }
#
# It never fired locally because this working copy happens to hold LF, which is
# exactly the shape of bug that only a clean checkout on another host reveals.
#
# A harness whose one job is determinism cannot have its own source change shape
# depending on who cloned it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The two that genuinely need CRLF: Windows shell wrappers are parsed by cmd.exe,
# which does not accept bare LF for some constructs.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary, so Git never tries to normalise them. A "corrected" byte in an APK or a
# keystore is a signature mismatch, and the fixture APK's whole value is that it
# is reproducible.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webm binary
*.mp4 binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.apk binary
*.jar binary
*.dex binary
*.keystore binary
*.pdf binary
